9rie\").. 24 July. George Alagiah, 67, journalist and presenter (BBC News), bowel cancer.. Trevor Francis, 67, footballer, heart attack. ", "syn_qa": [{"Q": "Who is stepping back from the planned investigation into how Richard Sharp got the job as BBC chairman?", "A": "William Shawcross", "S": "William Shawcross, the commissioner for public appointments, steps back from the planned investigation into how Richard Sharp got the job as BBC chairman because of previous contact between them."}, {"Q": "What is the reason for the increase in people not working due to a long-term health condition?", "A": "The rise is attributed to an increase in mental health problems among young people, and an increase in people suffering back and neck problems as a result of working at home.", "S": "The rise is attributed to an increase in mental health problems among young people, and an increase in people suffering back and neck problems as a result of working at home."}, {"Q": "Who is the new investigator appointed to take on the inquiry into how Richard Sharp got the job as BBC chairman?", "A": "Another investigator", "S": "William Shawcross, the commissioner for public appointments, steps back from the planned investigation into how Richard Sharp got the job as BBC chairman because of previous contact between them. Another investigator will be appointed to take on the inquiry.."}, {"Q": "Who was the first woman Speaker of the House of Commons?", "A": "Betty Boothroyd, Baroness Boothroyd", "S": "Betty Boothroyd, Baroness Boothroyd, 93, British politician, first woman Speaker of the House of Commons (1992\u20132000)."}, {"Q": "Who was handed the findings of an investigation into bullying allegations against Deputy Prime Minister Dominic Raab?", "A": "Prime Minister Rishi Sunak", "S": "Prime Minister Rishi Sunak is handed the findings of an investigation into bullying allegations against Deputy Prime Minister Dominic Raab.."}, {"Q": "What was the outcome of the 2023 Eurovision Song Contest?", "A": "Sweden's Loreen won the contest with the song \"Tattoo\".", "S": "The final of the 2023 Eurovision Song Contest takes place in Liverpool. The contest is won by Sweden's Loreen with the song \"Tattoo\", who becomes only the second person and the first woman to win the contest twice."}, {"Q": "Who succeeds Nicola Sturgeon as Leader of the SNP?", "A": "Humza Yousaf", "S": "Humza Yousaf succeeds Nicola Sturgeon as Leader of the SNP, after defeating rivals Kate Forbes and Ash Regan in a leadership election."}, {"Q": "What did Matt Hancock suggest to ensure people would comply with COVID-19 regulations?", "A": "He suggested to \"frighten the pants off everyone\".", "S": "Hancock appears to suggest they should \"frighten the pants off everyone\", while in another conversation, head of the civil service Simon Case suggests the \"fear/guilt factor\" is an important element of the government's messaging."}, {"Q": "What was the reason for HSBC's decision to vacate its 45-storey tower in Canary Wharf?", "A": "An increase in remote work and less need for in-person office work.", "S": "The move is attributed to an increase in remote work and less need for in-person office work."}, {"Q": "What was the reason for the delay in the construction of the Birmingham to Crewe leg of HS2?", "A": "To save costs.", "S": "The UK government announces a two-year delay in the construction of the Birmingham to Crewe leg of HS2 in order to save costs."}, {"Q": "Who is the new Chairman of the BBC?", "A": "Richard Sharp", "S": "Richard Sharp resigns as Chairman of the BBC over his breach of the BBC's rules regarding public appointments after failing to declare his connection to a loan secured by former Prime Minister Boris Johnson worth \u00a3800,000."}, {"Q": "Who is suspended by the BBC?", "A": "The presenter accused of paying a 17-year-old for sexually explicit photos.", "S": "The BBC subsequently confirms it has suspended the presenter and referred the matter to the police."}, {"Q":